00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:13.150
I think those who get an
abortion most of the time,

00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:15.300
it's because they need to.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:17.860
- It's a harmful narrative on
both sides of the conversation

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:19.930
to say that, you know,
women celebrate abortion.

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:21.130
I think it creates a prejudice

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:23.270
around women who do get abortions.

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:25.080
And I don't think that it's good

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:28.479
to kind of the decision of abortion

00:01:28.479 --> 00:01:31.057
from either side, from
the perspective, so.

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:32.723
- Can the disagree step forward?

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:40.120
- I think if you asked me this question,

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:41.700
maybe several years ago,

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.640
I would've said nobody likes abortion,

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:44.780
but I think in today's climate,

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:46.240
it is much more celebrated.

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:47.270
As a pro-life person,

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:48.103
I've had people tell me

00:01:48.103 --> 00:01:50.840
that they will dedicate
their next abortion to me

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:52.040
instead of helping women,

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:53.600
they will have an abortion.

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:56.590
- I've heard very
similar responses to you.

00:01:56.590 --> 00:02:00.040
Things like I'll donate to
planned parenthood in your name.

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:02.620
And there's other pages
like Shout Your Abortion

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:06.620
that openly celebrates abortion rights.

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:08.150
- Yeah, I celebrate abortion

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:11.040
and I think that campaigns
like Shout Your Abortion

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:13.510
aren't about like getting in your face,

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:16.760
but women who choose to have abortions

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:18.800
suffer a lot of stigma and trauma

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:21.140
from people who stand outside clinics

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:25.910
and have grotesque images
and literally, you know,

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:29.210
damning your soul abortion

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:33.280
as a medical procedure and resource

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:35.220
is something that I do celebrate.

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:36.670
It's a human right

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:38.393
and I love abortion.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.460
My name is Rocky You SheHer,

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:45.400
pronounced I'm from Austin, Texas.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.780
And I am very pro-abortion.

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:51.500
I think that legislation
like SB-Eight opens the door

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:54.210
and the path towards handing over

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:56.320
our bodily autonomy to the state.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:59.900
I don't understand how anyone can justify

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:01.260
using their personal beliefs

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:03.633
to take away the rights of others.

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:07.940
- My name's Abby, I'm
from Orlando, Florida.

00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:10.410
And I'm an abolitionist of human abortion.

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:13.250
We have to ask the question
of what makes humans valuable.

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:16.340
So because my world view as a Christian

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:18.760
gives me a foundation for human worth.

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:20.800
And because I believe scientifically

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.490
fetuses are human beings
on the moon of conception,

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:24.683
I am against abortion.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:30.753
- Biological fathers should
have an equal say in abortions.

00:03:40.747 --> 00:03:41.580
- Well, I think so.

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:42.510
I mean, it's consistency.

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:44.650
Like if we're defining that as a life,

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:47.950
if it is a life to put
a kid up for adoption,

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:49.600
both parents have to agree.

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:52.960
- I agree, I have talked to lots of women

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:53.793
who've had abortions

00:03:53.793 --> 00:03:55.090
and I've talked to lots of men

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:57.610
who are hurting, their
they're completely heartbroken

00:03:57.610 --> 00:03:58.610
they would've raised the baby.

00:03:58.610 --> 00:03:59.780
They wanted to raise baby.

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:01.890
They begged for the life of the baby

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:04.400
and they obviously
created the baby together

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:06.550
but only one of them gets to decide

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:09.100
if their child gets to live or die.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:11.490
- I would like to think
from more of a honestly

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:14.560
feminist perspective,
men have responsibility

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:16.280
as the other parent of that child.

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:17.970
Ironically enough, a lot of the times

00:04:17.970 --> 00:04:21.100
when pro-choice people put
the focus on the woman,

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:22.470
they strict the man

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:25.120
of all his parental rights
and responsibilities.

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:26.220
And I think that's why actually

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:28.580
a lot of men who are
pro-choice, are pro-choice

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:29.720
because they don't wanna have

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:31.080
those fatherly responsibilities

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:33.980
that they will have
once the child is born.

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:34.813
- You've left us, man.

00:04:34.813 --> 00:04:35.925
I wanna know why.

00:04:35.925 --> 00:04:37.125
- (indistinct) struggle.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:42.040
- I'm mad conflicted about this

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:44.251
because I strongly feel like a man

00:04:44.251 --> 00:04:47.840
should not have control over what a woman

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:49.420
does with her body.

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:51.440
I more so have an issue

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:55.180
with when a man doesn't
actually want that baby.

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:58.540
She wants it and then expects

00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:01.520
this man to like be the ultimate provider

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:05.410
and child care and all
this extra stuff, right?

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:08.080
But in the case of it, the man wanted it,

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:10.360
the baby and a woman didn't want it,

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:11.850
he has no say so.

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:14.300
I think that's (indistinct) up dynamic.

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:16.750
So that's why I was going back and forth.

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:17.600
- Well, you should have stayed then.

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:20.590
It sounds like you're for men
having more rights than that.

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:22.470
- I just can't force
women and be like, no,

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:23.590
you have to do this.

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:24.680
Cause I think it's (indistinct) up

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:25.513
it's her body.

00:05:25.513 --> 00:05:27.400
- But it's also a child's life in there.

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:28.260
It's not just her body.

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:29.359
It's a child's life.

00:05:29.359 --> 00:05:30.860
- And it's also your son or daughter.

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:32.790
- I think truly in my eyes,

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:34.160
it's like, it's my body.

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:35.370
I get to do what I want with it.

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:37.410
And I don't think anyone
including the person,

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:39.130
the other person who's involved

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:41.000
should have a say whether I wanna keep it

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:42.850
or whether I want to get an abortion.

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:48.190
- My name is Asher,
currently reside in Las Vegas

00:05:48.190 --> 00:05:49.780
and I'm for pro-abortion.

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:52.260
I used to be against abortion

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:57.030
until an unwanted
pregnancy happened to me.

00:05:57.030 --> 00:05:58.450
If you know for a fact

00:05:58.450 --> 00:06:00.220
that you're not even
gonna be the best parent

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:03.070
for that child or you can't
provide for that child,

00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:04.170
or maybe you're just fearful

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:06.230
and don't wanna pop a child outta you

00:06:06.230 --> 00:06:08.220
or just whatever reason that you have.

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:11.070
I feel like you shouldn't
have to go through that.

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:13.720
You still have that choice
over your life, your body.

00:06:15.223 --> 00:06:16.863
- I have had an abortion.

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:27.550
- A few months ago

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:31.220
I found out that I was pregnant.

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:32.792
So when I imagined myself

00:06:32.792 --> 00:06:36.260
finding out I was pregnant
for the first time

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:38.740
I wanted it be celebrated.

00:06:38.740 --> 00:06:42.900
And in that moment I
felt such severe anxiety

00:06:43.898 --> 00:06:48.898
and having that, I felt,
like the entire time

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:53.200
I was just in a lot of
emotional pain, grieving.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:56.050
I was debating about myself,

00:06:56.050 --> 00:06:58.590
about how I would be looked at

00:06:58.590 --> 00:07:00.810
or how I would view myself

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:02.633
after getting the procedure done.

00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:05.880
- I ain't gonna lie, I'm nervous.

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:07.610
So I'm be real careful in my words.

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:10.070
Clearly as a man, I
can't have an abortion,

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:15.070
but my girlfriend,
we've had two abortions.

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:17.670
She didn't really want to have a baby.

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:19.180
I didn't really want to have a baby.

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:20.400
And I know for me,

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:23.900
I don't want to be that seen
as that deadbeat father person,

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:28.900
but I knew I wasn't really
trying to sacrifice my own dreams

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:30.860
or what I was trying to accomplish

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:32.530
to be a dad at that point.

00:07:32.530 --> 00:07:34.800
- I think that's definitely
like one of the biggest things

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:38.610
to consider because I wasn't
in any kind of position

00:07:38.610 --> 00:07:40.110
to be a mother, you know?

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:40.943
So it's like,

00:07:40.943 --> 00:07:42.840
I wanna get my shit together

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:44.340
before I can have a baby

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:46.633
and give it a life that it deserves.

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:50.120
When I found out I was pregnant,

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:52.480
the person that I was with
at the time, they were like,

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:54.060
I will support you in every way,

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:57.110
but I will not be able to be there for you

00:07:57.110 --> 00:07:58.890
if you decide to keep it.

00:07:58.890 --> 00:08:02.270
And that definitely influenced my choice.

00:08:02.270 --> 00:08:05.260
It was one of the hardest
decisions I've ever had to make.

00:08:05.260 --> 00:08:07.320
I like to think I'm a pretty generous,

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:09.600
like loving person in the
names that I've been called

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:10.980
for even getting one.

00:08:10.980 --> 00:08:13.623
I've gotten evil, psychotic, demented.

00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:17.030
My name is Christine.

00:08:17.030 --> 00:08:21.160
I'm from Denver and I am
on the anti-abortion side.

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:22.470
So when I was 20 years old,

00:08:22.470 --> 00:08:23.590
I was a college student

00:08:23.590 --> 00:08:26.250
and I found myself in
an unplanned pregnancy.

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:29.020
And I was pressured to abort very heavily,

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:33.010
not only by my child's father,
but by those around me.

00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:35.380
And I heard my son's heartbeat

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:38.740
and there was no debate, it was a life.

00:08:38.740 --> 00:08:40.740
His life was not mine to take.

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:42.870
This is part of why I am very pro-life

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:45.190
because I know many women
are pressured to abort

00:08:45.190 --> 00:08:46.920
when they don't want to.

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:48.620
- Can the disagree a step forward?

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:57.570
- Your story is absolutely
powerful and your story as well.

00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:00.950
I think something we
probably all can agree on

00:09:00.950 --> 00:09:04.720
is abortion usually is a
symptom of a bigger problem,

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:08.280
whether it's finances, whether
it's stability of housing,

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:10.210
whether it's relationship issues,

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:13.900
my perspective is that
we address those issues

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:15.990
instead of ending the life of a child.

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:19.930
- I disagree, I don't think
that abortion is a symptom.

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:22.580
People should be able to access abortion

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:26.700
when, how, wherever they want or need.

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:28.750
I don't think that it's
a problem to be fixed.

00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:31.130
I think that is still stigmatizing.

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:33.530
- But I think the biggest thing is that

00:09:33.530 --> 00:09:35.470
there are birth control methods out there,

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:37.660
and abortion should not
be a birth control method.

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:39.620
I think that that's very critical.

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:42.710
And to hear that, you know,
you weren't celebrated,

00:09:42.710 --> 00:09:44.950
I think life should be
celebrated with everybody.

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:46.720
- I'd like to call
attention to that point too.

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:49.530
Just the fact of using
abortion as birth control.

00:09:49.530 --> 00:09:52.330
I thank you for everyone
sharing their stories so far.

00:09:52.330 --> 00:09:54.840
I didn't step forward, I
haven't had an abortion myself.

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:56.410
But I am a survey ever of rape.

00:09:56.410 --> 00:09:57.870
I was on birth control at the time

00:09:57.870 --> 00:10:00.680
and I still made the
decision with my medical team

00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:02.660
that birth control is not a
hundred percent effective.

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:05.080
And I wanted access to
emergency contraceptive

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:06.330
to take on top of that.

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:09.910
And had that pregnancy or
any of those methods failed,

00:10:09.910 --> 00:10:11.550
I would've chosen to have an abortion

00:10:11.550 --> 00:10:14.640
and I'm very grateful that I
had access to those resources

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:17.500
and I'm so mindful that
and many women who don't.

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:19.640
- Well, I think it gets down
to the heart of the issue here.

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:21.200
You know, what is the unborn?

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:24.050
Which scientifically the
embryo is from conception,

00:10:24.050 --> 00:10:26.970
a living whole organism with distinct DNA.

00:10:26.970 --> 00:10:27.803
As a Christian,

00:10:27.803 --> 00:10:29.460
I come from a worldview that says that

00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:32.650
every human being is,
has dignity and worth.

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:36.280
- Not to disrespect any
religion in general,

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:37.450
but in my eyes,

00:10:37.450 --> 00:10:39.810
that's just pushing a belief onto someone

00:10:39.810 --> 00:10:44.445
rather than actually stating
a real concrete fact.

00:10:44.445 --> 00:10:47.100
- So, scientifically I'm
pro-life because of science,

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:47.933
not because of religion.

00:10:47.933 --> 00:10:49.320
But scientifically, I believe that life

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:50.230
does start at conception.

00:10:50.230 --> 00:10:51.560
I don't think it makes sense to put life

00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:54.350
beginning at any other
place during pregnancy,

00:10:54.350 --> 00:10:56.280
doing so usually ends up saying

00:10:56.280 --> 00:10:59.060
that the already born
in person isn't alive,

00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:01.300
such as consciousness,
heartbeat, et cetera.

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:02.980
There are many pro-life people here

00:11:02.980 --> 00:11:04.940
here from the science perspective

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:09.113
who are not led by religious
motives at all, or partially.

00:11:11.930 --> 00:11:14.090
I am Ayala, I am 18 years old.

00:11:14.090 --> 00:11:15.870
I am from Charlotte, North Carolina.

00:11:15.870 --> 00:11:17.970
And I am anti-abortion.

00:11:17.970 --> 00:11:20.690
One misconception that I
deal with pretty frequently

00:11:20.690 --> 00:11:24.410
is that we are all
Christian, white, old men.

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:28.350
And as a, you know, Jewish woman younger,

00:11:28.350 --> 00:11:30.870
I really want more voices
like mine to be seen

00:11:30.870 --> 00:11:32.640
in the anti-abortion movement

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:34.160
because I think we have new perspectives

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:36.190
that would help kind of bridge the gap

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:38.390
and have us find a little
bit of middle ground

00:11:38.390 --> 00:11:40.383
between our two opposing sides.

00:11:41.390 --> 00:11:43.053
- Abortion is murder.

00:11:50.170 --> 00:11:51.280
- I think it is murder.

00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:55.900
I think for the abortionist
more so than the woman,

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:58.520
I think a lot of women
don't necessarily know

00:11:58.520 --> 00:12:00.650
exactly how an abortion
procedure is formed.

00:12:00.650 --> 00:12:02.650
I've had a girl even
tell me that at 20 weeks

00:12:02.650 --> 00:12:05.370
a baby is just a clump of
cells and that's just not true.

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:07.520
I do believe now there might
be cases where, you know,

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:09.040
some women might be unaware

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:11.770
of what's going on in an abortion.

00:12:11.770 --> 00:12:12.660
But by and large,

00:12:12.660 --> 00:12:14.570
I think especially with
the advent of the internet

00:12:14.570 --> 00:12:15.870
and so much education out there,

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:17.782
many of them do know that the life,

00:12:17.782 --> 00:12:19.750
