00:22:38.400 --> 00:22:39.333
- All right, well.

00:22:40.276 --> 00:22:41.493
- That ain't never going to change.

00:22:41.493 --> 00:22:43.700
- I think of course
they'll continue to happen.

00:22:43.700 --> 00:22:46.160
Law doesn't mean that
something is not gonna happen

00:22:46.160 --> 00:22:46.993
at all anymore.

00:22:46.993 --> 00:22:48.340
Just like rape, just like murder,

00:22:48.340 --> 00:22:49.840
just like anything else we've outlawed.

00:22:49.840 --> 00:22:51.890
Just because they're still going to happen

00:22:51.890 --> 00:22:53.560
doesn't make it right.

00:22:53.560 --> 00:22:57.060
- But if you criminalize doctors

00:22:57.060 --> 00:22:59.040
and abortion providers, right?

00:22:59.040 --> 00:23:01.060
That means we no longer have providers.

00:23:01.060 --> 00:23:03.630
That means abortion is
no longer an option.

00:23:03.630 --> 00:23:06.550
And that by default the
way that this country

00:23:06.550 --> 00:23:09.770
and especially my state
legislates will mean,

00:23:09.770 --> 00:23:10.603
and it has happened.

00:23:10.603 --> 00:23:14.600
We have precedent, a woman
who tries to self induce

00:23:14.600 --> 00:23:17.430
or who tries other non-medical methods

00:23:17.430 --> 00:23:18.280
to have an abortion

00:23:18.280 --> 00:23:20.600
can and has been criminalized.

00:23:20.600 --> 00:23:25.070
What is the policy that
doesn't just absolutely

00:23:25.070 --> 00:23:28.890
take away the right that people have

00:23:28.890 --> 00:23:30.490
to access an abortion

00:23:30.490 --> 00:23:33.430
regardless of what their beliefs are.

00:23:33.430 --> 00:23:34.307
- If that child is a human being

00:23:34.307 --> 00:23:36.000
deserving of the right to life,

00:23:36.000 --> 00:23:37.160
then yes, it should be criminalized

00:23:37.160 --> 00:23:39.450
just like murder of two year
olds and five year olds.

00:23:39.450 --> 00:23:41.150
And adults is criminalized, right?

00:23:41.150 --> 00:23:43.384
- But that's so different though.

00:23:43.384 --> 00:23:47.210
You have people that's two
years old, already out the womb,

00:23:47.210 --> 00:23:48.470
they been here for years, right?

00:23:48.470 --> 00:23:49.600
And then you got these cells.

00:23:49.600 --> 00:23:50.660
- Can I ask you something?

00:23:50.660 --> 00:23:51.493
- Go ahead.

00:23:51.493 --> 00:23:52.820
- When does it stop
being a clump of cells.

00:23:52.820 --> 00:23:56.530
- Personally, I'm not worried
about the clump of cells.

00:23:56.530 --> 00:23:58.070
- Decades of medical research

00:23:58.070 --> 00:24:00.487
has not been able to land on that answer.

00:24:00.487 --> 00:24:01.990
- And I'm trying to answer your question.

00:24:01.990 --> 00:24:02.823
As far as cells...

00:24:02.823 --> 00:24:03.656
- Do you believe that abortion

00:24:03.656 --> 00:24:05.830
should be allowed on
nine months of pregnancy?

00:24:05.830 --> 00:24:08.740
- I do feel that's a bit more extreme.

00:24:08.740 --> 00:24:11.499
So I will agree on that as a..

00:24:11.499 --> 00:24:14.580
- But let's not act like
women are just deciding

00:24:14.580 --> 00:24:17.620
to get abortions at
like during their second

00:24:17.620 --> 00:24:18.770
or third trimester.

00:24:18.770 --> 00:24:20.630
And the woman who are doing it,

00:24:20.630 --> 00:24:23.860
that's either that they're
going to die giving birth

00:24:23.860 --> 00:24:26.300
or it's under some men to circumstances,

00:24:26.300 --> 00:24:28.450
cause I doubt even myself,

00:24:28.450 --> 00:24:30.280
I doubt that I would get to a six month,

00:24:30.280 --> 00:24:31.671
seven month mark and then decide

00:24:31.671 --> 00:24:33.920
I don't wanna make this commitment.

00:24:33.920 --> 00:24:36.360
I feel like there's a
lot of this conversation.

00:24:36.360 --> 00:24:37.973
Like when does it become wrong?

00:24:40.080 --> 00:24:42.650
As if we're actually
going to get an abortion

00:24:42.650 --> 00:24:43.613
at that time.

00:24:44.810 --> 00:24:46.560
- A lot of the,

00:24:46.560 --> 00:24:49.540
what pro-life people
would consider hostile

00:24:49.540 --> 00:24:51.850
pro-choice comments and things like that

00:24:51.850 --> 00:24:55.043
are a response to hostile pro-life people.

00:24:55.043 --> 00:24:56.660
And I think that doesn't
get talked about in our side

00:24:56.660 --> 00:24:58.340
because we don't like to fight each other.

00:24:58.340 --> 00:24:59.330
But I think it's an important point

00:24:59.330 --> 00:25:01.800
because I've seen absolutely
disgraceful comments

00:25:01.800 --> 00:25:02.926
made towards women

00:25:02.926 --> 00:25:04.610
who are going into clinics, you know,

00:25:04.610 --> 00:25:07.160
who are obviously in a
very traumatizing situation

00:25:07.160 --> 00:25:09.030
and you don't know what
that woman is going through.

00:25:09.030 --> 00:25:10.540
And they're shouting obscenities at her.

00:25:10.540 --> 00:25:11.680
And that's appalling.

00:25:11.680 --> 00:25:13.370
And I think that we need
to take responsibility

00:25:13.370 --> 00:25:15.260
as pro-life people to understand

00:25:15.260 --> 00:25:16.580
they've experienced so much hurt

00:25:16.580 --> 00:25:17.617
from our side of the community.

00:25:17.617 --> 00:25:18.670
- And I agree with that.

00:25:18.670 --> 00:25:20.837
I think, but from our
side of the aisle folks

00:25:20.837 --> 00:25:22.160
who are very passionate

00:25:22.160 --> 00:25:23.230
because they believe that's a life,

00:25:23.230 --> 00:25:24.080
they believe that's a baby

00:25:24.080 --> 00:25:26.680
and they wanna do everything
they can to save that child.

00:25:26.680 --> 00:25:28.810
But I agree that our
rhetoric needs to be there

00:25:28.810 --> 00:25:30.610
as a resource and another option.

00:25:30.610 --> 00:25:33.150
And we can do that peacefully
and respectfully as well.

00:25:33.150 --> 00:25:35.640
- I think on any side of
any controversial issue,

00:25:35.640 --> 00:25:37.700
you're always gonna have those extremists,

00:25:37.700 --> 00:25:40.300
same thing on the pro-abortion side,

00:25:40.300 --> 00:25:41.470
people are always gonna have feelings

00:25:41.470 --> 00:25:43.700
and people are always gonna
fight on that level, right?

00:25:43.700 --> 00:25:44.960
But I think it's about coming up here

00:25:44.960 --> 00:25:48.650
and saying like what
actually makes common sense

00:25:48.650 --> 00:25:51.600
and how do we come up with policy

00:25:51.600 --> 00:25:54.140
that doesn't force folks

00:25:54.140 --> 00:25:57.820
to live by other people's values.

00:25:57.820 --> 00:26:00.737
(enchanting music)

